# Projects

Work in this repo happens in a **project**. Thalos is the default. Earth is
the **fixture**, not a tree.

- Thalos is the world being discovered. Development, `bun run preview`,
  `bun run sheet`, and `bun run export:td` run against it unless Earth is
  asked for. The project file holds the adopted **body** (and pipeline
  notes). It does not hold a seed or a gene bag.
- Earth is the present-day reference fixture. Use `--earth` or
  `--project=earth`, or `bun run check:earth`. No search, no variants. Its
  file authors body plus fixture knobs and the `'earth'` token so shaping
  can be tested on a known tectonic base.
- The app starts on a project page. Opening a project persists it
  (`planetgen.activeProject`); a restart resumes that project. Switching
  means going back to the project page — there is no in-workspace dropdown.
- A **variant** is a saved candidate: seed, body, gene draws, body **pins**,
  **ranges**, and a parent. Shuffle, a new seed, or an explore tile is a
  different planet — **Save** branches (child of **head**, even with no
  name). Tilt, pins, and genes on this seed are the same planet — Save
  writes a newer generation of the current version. A name labels a
  branch; it is not what makes one. The UI word is Save, never Update.
  Explore likes write **ranges** to the current version as they go. Pins
  are body-only. Earth has no variants.
- Artifacts belong to a variant: `preview/<project>/v/<id>/`, catalog at
  `preview/<project>/variants.json`. Earth and a project with no variant
  still use `preview/<project>/`. Listing without a variant id does not
  walk `v/`. Loading another project or variant must not show the last
  one's tiles.
- CLI with no seed uses the committed variant if there is one, else a
  working planet from the adopted body.
- Do not treat the generator's Earth-calibrated DEFAULTS as a third project.
  Those are the unmarked baseline the body sits on.
